#: src/whats-the-relationship-between-just-and-cargo-build-scripts.md:1
msgid "What’s the relationship between Just and Cargo build scripts?"
msgstr ""

#: src/whats-the-relationship-between-just-and-cargo-build-scripts.md:3
msgid ""
"[`cargo` build scripts](http://doc.crates.io/build-script.html) have a "
"pretty specific use, which is to control how `cargo` builds your Rust "
"project. This might include adding flags to `rustc` invocations, building an "
"external dependency, or running some kind of codegen step."
msgstr ""

#: src/whats-the-relationship-between-just-and-cargo-build-scripts.md:8
msgid ""
"`just`, on the other hand, is for all the other miscellaneous commands you "
"might run as part of development. Things like running tests in different "
"configurations, linting your code, pushing build artifacts to a server, "
"removing temporary files, and the like."
msgstr ""

#: src/whats-the-relationship-between-just-and-cargo-build-scripts.md:13
msgid ""
"Also, although `just` is written in Rust, it can be used regardless of the "
"language or build system your project uses."
msgstr ""
